    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI have been using the builtin jump2d opts, but I have found writing my own spotter challenging.\r\nIf you don't mind, could you assist me in writing it? \r\n\r\n- I had tried to copy parts of the code for builtin opts, but I don't know how to limit the user input to two characters.\r\n\r\nI have also found the builtin jump by query option to be great, but it is case-sensitive. Is there a way to make it case-insensitive?\r\n\r\nThanks for the awesome plugin!\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have been using the builtin jump2d opts, but I have found writing my own spotter challenging.<br>\nIf you don't mind, could you assist me in writing it?</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I had tried to copy parts of the code for builtin opts, but I don't know how to limit the user input to two characters.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have also found the builtin jump by query option to be great, but it is case-sensitive. Is there a way to make it case-insensitive?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the awesome plugin!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello,\nI have been using the builtin jump2d opts, but I have found writing my own spotter challenging.\nIf you don't mind, could you assist me in writing it?\n\nI had tried to copy parts of the code for builtin opts, but I don't know how to limit the user input to two characters.\n\nI have also found the builtin jump by query option to be great, but it is case-sensitive. Is there a way to make it case-insensitive?\nThanks for the awesome plugin!",
